Author: JimmyShi22 <417711026@qq.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 12:16:01 2026 +0800

    Map the lookup keys to the committed rounding digits (partial progress)
    
    The lookup key plan now comes from the trusted rounding layout: every committed digit slot of every position becomes a key entry that reads the physical cell of that position rounding message, the six value slots are excluded, and the remaining keys use the public padding byte. A helper derives the minimal key-bit and multiplicity-plane counts from the digit count. The hidden fixture reads the real rounding messages through this map.
    
    The lookup commit-plan sizing from the parent plan and the BAT/FOLD registration of the lookup claims are not part of this step.

